   "severity": "info",
   "ruleId": "HEATER_BYPASS",
   "text": "Plumb in a heater bypass while you are at it. Isolate a leaking or failed heater without shutting the pump down, so the pool keeps circulating and chlorinating. It also protect the copper heat exchanger when pH drops below about 7.0 — acidic water erodes the core and can stain the pool. And it cut back pressure for the ~95% of the time the heater is not in use; heat pumps restrict more than gas heaters because of smaller internal piping."
